  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 49922f05034be6f4fa205a70b2ad0a2e, type: 3}
  m_Name: C_P_Rapax
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodexPageData
  Title: Rapax
  Version: 1.0.0
  Icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 95e5cbf06f9cbf84282795b8526a63c6, type: 3}
  TagLine: The only thing a predator fears is a bigger predator
  ContentHeaders:
  - Activation Criteria
  - Ability
  - Lore Entry
  Content:
  - Have at least 5 Rapax Programs active in memory. The effect will then stay active.
  - '**5 Programs:** Heal by 5% on kill, and reload weapon to maximum capacity.

    **7
    Programs:** Heal effect increased to 7.5%.'
  - "When humans first learned to walk the land, they learned from what was here
    before them. Nature, and animals. They learned from the claws of the bears that
    sharp things hurt, the shell of the turtles how to protect themselves, and the
    fish on how to swin.\n\nI don't know what they were thinking when they did this,
    but they did it. To me, I would think learning from each other would be faster
    but I'm a machine, so what do I know?\n\nAnyways, have this suite. Its all about
    making you slightly better at one thing at a time. Just don't expect much. They
    uh... The dev's were still learning how to work a computer when they made these.
    Don't blame me if you catch fire as a result of running one of them. \n"
